/-! ## §1 — THE SELF-BLIND COUNT `finrank ℚ Uhol = 3` read across three arc-P sectors, with teeth. -/

/-- NEW LEMMA (the P6 tooth for §1). The triality generation cycle does NOT close at the WRONG count
    `2`: `trialityHom gcyc ^ 2 ≠ 1`. `gcyc = finRotate 3` has order exactly `3`, so its square is a
    nontrivial permutation, and `trialityHom` is injective (N432), hence `trialityHom gcyc ^ 2 ≠ 1`.
    Physics-words-removable: a permutation homomorphism's square is not the identity. -/
theorem trialityHom_gcyc_sq_ne_one : trialityHom gcyc ^ 2 ≠ 1 := by
  rw [← trialityHom.map_pow]
  intro h
  have hg : gcyc ^ 2 = 1 := trialityHom_injective (by rw [h, trialityHom.map_one])
  exact absurd hg (by decide)

/-- ★★ THE SELF-BLIND COUNT THREAD (P3 ⊗ P4 ⊗ P6, NEW — extends P7's abstract P3⊗P6 weld by adding
    P4). The SAME derived count `finrank ℚ Uhol` (the derivation-stabilizer dimension = the count of
    directions the fold's self-look-back cannot resolve) reads THREE arc-P sectors at once:
      • P3 — the SU(2)²·U(1) anomaly cancels at that count (`su2_mixed_anomaly_cancels`);
      • P4 — the weak-mixing normalization is forced to `3/8` from the banked traces AT that count
        (`weinberg_normalization_forced`);
      • P6 — the triality generation cycle closes with exponent that count
        (`trialityHom gcyc ^ (finrank ℚ Uhol) = 1`).
    The anomaly-cancelling colour count, the Weinberg trace depth, and the triality cycle order are
    ONE self-blind count. Physics-words-removable: at a shared natural number `finrank ℚ Uhol`, a
    complement-indexed rational sum is `0`, a trace ratio is `3/8`, and a permutation homomorphism's
    power is `1`. -/
theorem selfblind_count_reads_three_sectors :
    su2MixedCoeff (Module.finrank ℚ Uhol) (Module.finrank ℚ singlet) = 0
    ∧ weinberg (1 * isospinTrace (Module.finrank ℚ Uhol + Module.finrank ℚ singlet)
          (∑ i : Fin 2, (fund2Weight i) ^ 2))
        (1 * ladderChargeTrace (Module.finrank ℚ Uhol)) = 3 / 8
    ∧ trialityHom gcyc ^ (Module.finrank ℚ Uhol) = 1 :=
  ⟨su2_mixed_anomaly_cancels,
   weinberg_normalization_forced 1 (by norm_num),
   by rw [finrank_Uhol]; exact trialityHom_gcyc_order3⟩

/-- ★★ THE MULTI-NODE TEETH (NEW — never co-stated). Perturb the ONE shared count to the WRONG value
    `2` and TWO arc-P sectors break AT ONCE: P3's SU(2)²·U(1) anomaly no longer cancels
    (`su2_mixed_anomaly_wrong_colour`, `su2MixedCoeff 2 _ ≠ 0`) AND P6's triality cycle no longer
    closes (`trialityHom_gcyc_sq_ne_one`, `trialityHom gcyc ^ 2 ≠ 1`). The shared-count reading is
    genuinely load-bearing across nodes: the anomaly cancellation and the triality closure are not
    independent coincidences — they are the SAME count, and a wrong count kills both. Physics-words-
    removable: the argument `2` makes a rational sum nonzero AND a permutation's square `≠ 1`. -/
theorem wrong_count_breaks_anomaly_and_triality :
    su2MixedCoeff 2 (Module.finrank ℚ singlet) ≠ 0
    ∧ trialityHom gcyc ^ 2 ≠ 1 :=
  ⟨su2_mixed_anomaly_wrong_colour, trialityHom_gcyc_sq_ne_one⟩

/-! ## §2 — THE FOLD RETURN TURN `azimuthalTurn = 2·cutPi` exhibited inside the mass scale. -/

/-- ★★ THE FOLD-TURN THREAD (P1 ⊗ P2, NEW — P7's WELD 1 stopped at the opaque `minimalWrapRatio`;
    here the fold RETURN TURN is exhibited EXPLICITLY inside the absolute mass scale). The whole mass
    tower's anchor routes through the fold return turn `azimuthalTurn = 2·cutPi` (N328), divided by
    the DERIVED Born-channel count `1/α* = 42` (arc A) and the DERIVED wrap count `comarkCount = 9`
    (P1):
      `massScale = cutExp(−(azimuthalTurn·(1/α*)/comarkCount)) · ((cutCos foldPhase · s1BornProb)·1·cutCos(2/3))`.
    Welds P7's `massScale_anchored_on_wrap` (the mass scale factors through the minimal-wrap amplitude)
    with P1's `minimalWrap_exponent` (the exponent IS `azimuthalTurn·(1/α*)/comarkCount`) — the mass
    scale is the fold turn read at the fold's own two counts. No free scale. Physics-words-removable: a
    distinguished `Cut` factors as a `cutExp` of `azimuthalTurn` scaled by two derived rationals times a
    product of derived cosines and the banked survival fraction. -/
theorem massScale_through_fold_turn :
    Phys.Algebra.AbsMass.massScale
      = cutExp (-(azimuthalTurn * ((1 / alphaStar : ℚ) : Cut) / (comarkCount : Cut)))
          * ((cutCos foldPhase * ((s1BornProb : ℚ) : Cut)) * 1 * cutCos (2 / 3)) := by
  have hmr : minimalWrapRatio
      = cutExp (-(azimuthalTurn * ((1 / alphaStar : ℚ) : Cut) / (comarkCount : Cut))) := by
    unfold minimalWrapRatio; rw [minimalWrap_exponent]
  rw [Phys.Algebra.Reckoning.massScale_anchored_on_wrap, hmr]

/-! ## §3 — TWO DISTINCT DERIVED DIMENSIONS (the honest guard against "one magic number"). -/

/-- ★ TWO DISTINCT DERIVED DIMENSIONS (NEW). The EW wrap count `finrank ℚ spaceSub = 9` (P1, the F₄
    comark sum) and the colour/generation count `finrank ℚ Uhol = 3` are DIFFERENT derived integers.
    The reckoning does NOT rest on a single fitted number: it uses a small STRUCTURED set of
    separately-derived counts. Physics-words-removable: two `finrank`s are unequal (`9 ≠ 3`). -/
theorem two_derived_counts_distinct :
    Module.finrank ℚ spaceSub ≠ Module.finrank ℚ Uhol := by
  rw [finrank_spaceSub, finrank_Uhol]; decide

/-! ## §4 — THE CAPSTONE. -/

/-- ★★★ N### — THE ARC-P CONSOLIDATION (arc-P P8, the LAST node of arc P, THE FINAL RECKONING). Arc P
    read as ONE structure over the fold's TWO self-blindness measures:
      • THE SELF-BLIND COUNT `finrank ℚ Uhol` (`selfblind_count_reads_three_sectors`): the SAME derived
        count reads the anomaly cancellation (P3), the weak-mixing normalization (P4), AND the triality
        cycle order (P6) — with MULTI-NODE teeth (`wrong_count_breaks_anomaly_and_triality`: the wrong
        count `2` breaks P3 AND P6 at once);
      • THE FOLD RETURN TURN `azimuthalTurn` (`massScale_through_fold_turn`): the absolute mass scale
        routes through the fold turn divided by the derived channel count and wrap count (P1 ⊗ P2);
      • TWO DISTINCT DERIVED DIMENSIONS (`two_derived_counts_distinct`): the EW wrap count `9` and the
        colour/generation count `3` are different derived integers — a structured set, not one number.
    Every Standard-Model input class the reckoning derived is a reading of the fold's self-blindness in
    its two measures; the chain has ZERO free parameters. ⚠ THEOREM-route for the STRUCTURE (the three
    threads + teeth); the reading "arc P is the reckoning — the electroweak scale (P1), the mass
    spectrum (P2), the anomalies (P3), the θ-term + normalization (P4), the covariant divergence
    (P5/P5b — gravity, structurally distinct, named not conjoined), the triality group (P6), and the
    parameter-free certificate (P7) — every owed debt paid; zero free parameters" is the MECHANISM-grade
    closure statement (physics-words-removable prose over the cited banked capstones), never a
    load-bearing theorem. Physics-words-removable: arithmetic / linear-algebra facts about the banked
    derived `Cut` / ℚ-arena objects. -/
theorem arcP_consolidation :
    -- §1 the self-blind count reads three sectors, with multi-node teeth
    (su2MixedCoeff (Module.finrank ℚ Uhol) (Module.finrank ℚ singlet) = 0
      ∧ weinberg (1 * isospinTrace (Module.finrank ℚ Uhol + Module.finrank ℚ singlet)
            (∑ i : Fin 2, (fund2Weight i) ^ 2))
          (1 * ladderChargeTrace (Module.finrank ℚ Uhol)) = 3 / 8
      ∧ trialityHom gcyc ^ (Module.finrank ℚ Uhol) = 1)
    ∧ (su2MixedCoeff 2 (Module.finrank ℚ singlet) ≠ 0
      ∧ trialityHom gcyc ^ 2 ≠ 1)
    -- §2 the fold return turn is exhibited inside the mass scale
    ∧ (Phys.Algebra.AbsMass.massScale
        = cutExp (-(azimuthalTurn * ((1 / alphaStar : ℚ) : Cut) / (comarkCount : Cut)))
            * ((cutCos foldPhase * ((s1BornProb : ℚ) : Cut)) * 1 * cutCos (2 / 3)))
    -- §3 two distinct derived dimensions
    ∧ (Module.finrank ℚ spaceSub ≠ Module.finrank ℚ Uhol) :=
  ⟨selfblind_count_reads_three_sectors, wrong_count_breaks_anomaly_and_triality,
    massScale_through_fold_turn, two_derived_counts_distinct⟩

